13723	{"artifactId":"LLD-1f74c81f507dbe78-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-1f74c81f507dbe78-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:59:22.935Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream ask (c9: paged table, search with autocomplete and type dropdown instead of the dropdown; c10: an open document follows changes on disk, and an insrc review icon in line with the delivery board's) is designed, and nothing beyond them is built.","evidence":"The three asks map to ac3, ac1 and ac2, and each has a contract section (LIST VIEW, WATCH / RELOAD IN PLACE, ICON). The thing being replaced is real: the header is `<select id=\"insrc-docs-list\" aria-label=\"document\">` (docs-review-panel.ts:2085). The extra elements (reveal flag, notice line, saved view) come from the two earlier daemon reviews (c12, c13), not from new scope. No non-goal is stated upstream. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the header holds a select of every pending document, and the summary the host receives is { id, kind, title, status }.","evidence":"protocol.ts:53-58 declares `DocsArtifactSummary { id; kind; title; status }`. renderList (docs-review-panel.ts:1882-1887) appends one option per item to the select at :2085. The client maps only those four fields (docs-review-client.ts:118-123). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The open document is re-read only when it is opened, after a decision, or on the rebuilt shell's boot ping; the plugin watches no file.","evidence":"reopen() is called only from decide() (docs-review-panel.ts:1549, 1567, 1580) and from the empty-id 'open-doc' (`void refreshPending().then(reopen)`, :2158). A search for `createFileSystemWatcher` across vscode-plugin/src returns no match. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The review pane's tab and its command have no icon today, while the chat panel and the delivery board set a light/dark pair.","evidence":"package.json:100-103 declares insrc.chat.docsReview with only command, title and category; the neighbouring commands carry `icon: { light, dark }` (:94-97, :108-111). extension.ts:670-671 passes the review panel straight to webviewChannel with no iconPath, whereas the chat panel sets `panel.iconPath = { light, dark }` before `webviewChannel(panel)` (:560-565) and the board sets it in board-wiring.ts:59. .vscodeignore excludes src, tests and config but not media/. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-wiring.ts, vscode-plugin/.vscodeignore]","action":"None. The description of the chosen alternative in section 7.1 still mentions 'an optional tabIcon dep'; section 2 (no host change) is the one to build.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon already sends openQuestionCount and workItemId on each pending artifact, so the new summary fields need no daemon change.","evidence":"src/workflow/pending.ts:47-48: `readonly workItemId?: string; readonly openQuestionCount: number;`. toDescriptor sets openQuestionCount always and workItemId only when derived (:152-155). The client already imports PendingArtifact and drops both (docs-review-client.ts:118-123). Note: PENDING_KINDS (:39) has no BUILD, so the BUILD entry in the list's type order never matches a row; it is inert. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts]","action":"Optional: drop BUILD from the type order, or leave it as a harmless entry.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'.insrc/artifacts/<artifactId>.json' is the file a pending document's record and saved comments live in, so watching it catches a comment saved by another tool.","evidence":"pending.ts:11 names the store `.insrc/artifacts/<KIND>-<hash>.json` and :136 derives `artifactId = file.replace(/\\.json$/, '')`. Comments are read from that record: artifact-content.ts:228 `body['feedback']`. contentVersion is a hash of the rendered markdown only (:98-99, :239), which fits the design's rule that a JSON-only change reloads without the 'changed' line. I did not trace whether the id the delivery board passes to openArtifact is always this file identity. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/artifact-content.ts]","action":"None for pending rows. For board-opened documents, confirm at build that the evidence entry's artifactId is the store's file name.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"reopen() exists, re-reads the open document by its path, and runs under the openSeq / refreshSeq guards the watch's re-read is meant to reuse.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.ts:1503-1513: reopen() calls `openDoc(o.artifactId, { path: o.docPath, kind, readOnly: awaiting === undefined })`. openDoc bumps openSeq and drops a superseded answer (:1369, :1372, :1480); refreshPending does the same with refreshSeq (:1281, :1284). openDoc's options have no changed/reveal today, so both must be threaded through openDoc and reopen, as the design implies. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The four places the design names (a document is read, a failed open of another clears it, the panel is closed, dispose()) are every assignment of the host's open-document record.","evidence":"`opened` is assigned at exactly four sites in createDocsReviewHost: :1375 (successful read), :1483 (`if (opened?.artifactId !== artifactId) opened = undefined`), :2194 (onDidDispose) and :2211 (dispose()). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'Recorded, refused or failed' covers every way decide() settles, so a change remembered during a decision is always released.","evidence":"decide() has five exits: not the open document (:1539-1543), not awaiting review (:1545-1550), no docPath (:1552-1554), daemon call failed (:1559-1568), recorded (:1570-1580). The first three are host refusals, the fourth is the failure, the fifth the recording. The failure path re-reads the document only when its place in the list changed (:1567), which is the case the design's 'whether or not the decision re-read the document' covers. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Release the remembered change in a finally around the whole of decide(), so an exit added later cannot skip it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The draft writer is the only writer of the review shell's saved state today, and it writes an object holding only 'rv'.","evidence":"docs-review-comments.ts:252: `vs.setState({rv:all})`; rvStored (:247) reads only `s.rv`. No other setState exists in the review shell (the only other one in the plugin is the delivery board's, board-host.ts:321, which already merges with `Object.assign({},savedState(),…)`). The two call sites the design lists for the state change are therefore complete. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-comments.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Disposing and restarting the watch at every assignment of the record loses no file change.","evidence":"The record is reassigned on every successful read, including each re-read the watch itself starts (docs-review-panel.ts:1375). As written, every reload disposes both watchers and creates two new ones on the same paths. Whether VS Code delivers an event that lands between the dispose and the new watcher becoming live cannot be checked from the code; it needs a real VS Code. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Keep the existing watch when the new record's docPath and artifactId are unchanged; dispose and restart only when they differ.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A webview state saved by the earlier build (only 'rv') is read as before and gets the list defaults; the new summary fields are absent keys when the daemon sent none.","evidence":"rvStored tolerates any state shape and reads only `s.rv` (docs-review-comments.ts:247), so adding a 'list' key beside it does not disturb the drafts; rvLoad validates each saved draft (:254-258). The summary fields are optional additions to an interface whose only non-test users are protocol.ts, docs-review-client.ts and docs-review-panel.ts (search for DocsArtifactSummary). No daemon call or stored record changes. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-comments.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed re-read of the open document posts the 'unavailable' content and keeps the host's record; a failed open of another document clears the record.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.ts:1476-1494: the catch drops a superseded failure, then `if (opened?.artifactId !== artifactId) opened = undefined`, then posts `markdown: 'unavailable: …', blocked: true`. So the watch stays after a failed re-read and is dropped after a failed open of another document, as the design states. One path is not stated: an 'open-doc' for a row that is no longer pending is dropped with only a list refresh (:2161-2165); the row then disappears, which is unchanged behaviour. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Optional: add the stale-row press to the error cases (the list refreshes and the row goes).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed list read reaches the shell as an empty 'docs-list' plus a 'docs-content' with an empty artifact id, which the shell must treat as a notice rather than a document.","evidence":"postUnavailable (docs-review-panel.ts:1295-1305) posts `{ type: 'docs-list', artifacts: [] }` and then `{ type: 'docs-content', artifactId: '', markdown: 'docs-review unavailable: …' }`. Today the shell sends that through renderContent, which sets `shown=m;current=''` (:2058) and replaces the open document; the design's notice line removes that. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Route an empty-id 'docs-content' to the notice line before renderContent is reached, so `shown` is not overwritten.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to tests that the existing suites can carry: host tests over fakes, shell tests that run the real script, a baseline pin, and a wiring test over extension.ts.","evidence":"ac1, ac2 and ac3 each list proving tests in the acceptance mapping. The shell harness runs the real script with `new Function('document','window','marked','acquireVsCodeApi', script)` and a getState/setState pair (docs-review-panel.test.ts:1941-1947), so saved-state and view tests fit it; SHELL_BASELINE is pinned at :1235 and must move with the shell. A test of extension.ts wiring is done as a source scan elsewhere (freshness/__tests__/extension-wiring.test.ts:17, __tests__/activation.test.ts:86). The light/dark look of the icon is covered only by the hand check, which is the only place it can be seen. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/freshness/__tests__/extension-wiring.test.ts]","action":"None. Existing tests that look up 'insrc-docs-list' (:1868, :5757) will need updating with the header change, as step 4 says.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-13T15:59:22.935Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
